Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.99,0:00:09.78,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Domain Expansion: Chimera Shadow Garden.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.33,0:00:18.87,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Esoteric Technique: Hollow Wicker Basket! {supposed to be Secret Art? no that's a different word, maybe Esoteric Art?}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.33,0:00:27.01,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Hollow Wicker Basket is the origin \Nof New Shadow Style's Simple Domain.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.01,0:00:32.30,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,It possesses the ability to neutralize a domain \Nand counter its sure-hit effect.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.47,0:00:34.26,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Too bad!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.35,0:00:38.73,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,The Domain Extension that \NJogo and Hanami used in Shibuya
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.73,0:00:42.94,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,could have been infused \Nwith a sure-hit, sure-kill technique.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.86,0:00:47.86,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why can he still hit me? {Why is it hitting me?!}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.86,0:00:55.03,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,By deliberately omitting one, \Nthey freed up capacity to channel Gojo's technique,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.03,0:00:57.16,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,neutralizing his Limitless. {Infinity?}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.45,0:01:03.50,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,However, Hollow Wicker Basket and Simple Domain \Ncannot neutralize the cursed technique itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.96,0:01:12.43,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,They neutralize the barrier infused with \Nthe technique to nullify the sure-hit effect.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.01,0:01:18.39,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,However, Fushiguro's domain is incomplete.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.64,0:01:20.52,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Not so smug now, are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.52,0:01:22.35,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,You little shit!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.11,0:01:31.74,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,By transposing his domain onto the gymnasium itself, \Nhe managed to force it closed, {space of the } {"onto the gymnasium itself" already implies the space}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.74,0:01:34.62,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,but it's not infused with a sure-hit technique.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.24,0:01:37.87,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Don't think you've won!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.58,0:01:41.25,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}Now I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.25,0:01:47.17,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,At the moment, Chimera Shadow Garden simply \Nextends his Ten Shadows Technique,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.17,0:01:52.05,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,drawing out 120% of his potential. {potential mentioned!!!}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.68,0:01:57.56,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,However, that very imperfection \Nwas what caught Reggie Star off-guard.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.56,0:02:02.14,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}His clones and his {*}cursed beasts{*shikigami} \Nalready had physical forms before they hit me. {how does this lead to his conclusion on the next line?} {he sees them materialize before the hit, which means there's no sure-hit, because in a sure-hit domain attacks land automatically without physically reaching you, i think} {ok so he doesn't exactly seem them materialize before the hit, he observes that they already have tangible bodies before impact, and that leads to him concluding that there's no sure-hit effect}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.14,0:02:06.15,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}Which means this barrier \Nisn't infused with a sure-hit technique!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.15,0:02:10.65,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}The buff to his technique is nothing to scoff at, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.65,0:02:14.07,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is way worse than a regular sure-hit domain!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.07,0:02:17.83,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}If he summons that elephant here \Nand drenches me in water,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.83,0:02:20.87,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}it'll halve my options and seal my defeat.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.67,0:02:32.05,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}But I won't let that happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.05,0:02:35.01,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}That's just who I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.14,0:02:36.93,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Nue!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.81,0:02:43.31,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Too slow!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.27,0:02:48.77,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,I knew it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.36,0:02:57.32,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,I've been reinforcing my footing with cursed energy \N this whole time to avoid getting sucked in.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.95,0:03:05.29,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Everything below the surface of this domain \Nis your shadow, isn't it? {surface but specifically ground surface}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.54,0:03:10.67,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Must be convenient being able to \Nmove things in and out, even yourself. {CR: Being able to store and remove yourself and objects must be convenient.} {Must be convenient being able to move things in and out, even yourself.}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.67,0:03:13.30,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,But one thing nagged at me. {this part nags at me too...}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.30,0:03:15.72,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,"He doesn't have many weapons."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.72,0:03:19.05,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,I've only seen you use one paltry cursed tool.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.05,0:03:25.35,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Maybe it has low capacity, and you need to \Nreserve space for yourself at all times. {Either it has low capacity and you need to reserve space for yourself at all times,}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.35,0:03:32.57,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Or maybe you're forced to bear the weight \Nof everything stored in your shadow. {Or maybe you're forced to bear the weight of things stored in your shadow yourself.} {or you're forced to bear the weight of things stored in your shadow yourself.}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.65,0:03:35.49,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Looks like the latter was spot-on!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.03,0:03:39.49,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Now I've turned the design \Nof your domain against you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.82,0:03:44.83,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,With three passenger cars, \Nyour current weight is 2.4 tons.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.83,0:03:47.21,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Looks like your clones couldn't handle it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.21,0:03:50.34,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Maybe you can still use your {*}cursed beasts{*shikigami}?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.34,0:03:56.72,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Either way, I simply need to \Nwatch my footing and keep piling on
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.72,0:03:58.97,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,until you're crushed under your own weight.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.55,0:04:03.77,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Aren't you forgetting something? {CR: Are you stupid?}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.14,0:04:05.18,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.18,0:04:08.73,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,An incomplete domain is still a domain!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.69,0:04:12.94,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,There's shadow above you too!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.74,0:04:29.25,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Who's getting crushed first, Reggie?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.93,0:06:09.56,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,It's said that an average human \Nloses consciousness at five to six Gs.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.97,0:06:11.56,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,2.4 tons.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.19,0:06:19.48,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Assuming Fushiguro weighed 60 kilograms, \Nhe was currently bearing 40 Gs. {As Fushiguro weighs 60 kilograms, that means he's currently under 40 Gs.} {narrator doesn't know his weight for sure}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.49,0:06:27.20,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,In order to prevent his blood from pooling in his legs \Nand depriving his brain of blood flow,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.20,0:06:31.91,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Fushiguro lowered his posture and \Nreinforced his body with cursed energy,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.91,0:06:34.79,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,paying special attention to his legs.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.21,0:06:40.59,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,A mature African elephant weighs three to six tons.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.09,0:06:48.60,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,With the technique's precision boosted by his domain, \NMax Elephant's weight was faithfully recreated.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.01,0:06:54.81,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Reggie Star's right fibula and calcaneus \Nfractured under that weight.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.19,0:07:02.61,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Both of them faced the possibility \Nof being crushed to death at any second.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.07,0:07:06.03,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}I screwed up!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.03,0:07:08.91,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}I could have won if I'd kept the trucks in reserve!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.91,0:07:10.37,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}What do I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.37,0:07:15.08,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}I got splashed with some water, \Nbut I've still got my trump card.\h\h
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.08,0:07:19.17,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}I could slip into his shadow and \Nrecreate my trump card from the inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.17,0:07:21.38,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}That would crush him!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.46,0:07:24.42,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}No...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.42,0:07:26.84,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}Since he's not dismissing his domain,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.84,0:07:32.39,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}it's possible that anything swallowed by his shadow \Nremains trapped even after the domain is dismissed! {shorter: it means anything in his shadow is stuck there after he dismisses his domain!}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.02,0:07:36.94,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}What if I'm stuck in his shadow forever after he dies?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.69,0:07:40.19,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}What's it like inside the shadow, anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.19,0:07:43.82,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}It looks like liquid. \NCan I breathe in it? Will I float?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.61,0:07:48.57,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}No. Submerging into his shadow is too risky.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.57,0:07:51.37,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have to do it here and now.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.33,0:07:55.54,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have to pull out my trump card and activate it!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.71,0:08:02.63,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Contractual Re-Creation!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.44,0:08:24.15,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}I didn't make it in time!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.15,0:08:27.40,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}As I thought, there's no air inside the shadow!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.86,0:08:31.57,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}No buoyancy or resistance either!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.33,0:08:38.92,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm just... sinking!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.17,0:08:43.80,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}My consciousness... is fading...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.63,0:08:51.93,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}Not yet! Keep enduring! {Tough it out!} {CR: Endure it a little longer}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.93,0:08:54.85,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}Wait until he's dead before dismissing the domain!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.85,0:08:57.64,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then I can expel whatever's in my shadow!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.30,0:09:36.97,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,The things I recreate disappear \Nsoon after carrying out my command.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.97,0:09:40.23,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,I hadn't given the cars I sank a command yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.23,0:09:43.44,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Didn't want them disappearing, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.44,0:09:46.65,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,That meant I could still issue them a command.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.65,0:09:49.11,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,"Rise up and bring me to the surface!"
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.49,0:09:53.91,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,The weight of one car is gone, \Nbut that saved my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.95,0:10:01.46,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,I'll admit it. You're strong.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.08,0:10:07.34,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,However, {\i1}I{\i0} am stronger!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.34,0:10:10.80,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Contractual Re-Creation!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.89,0:10:21.39,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,A 132-square-meter, two-story wooden structure! {square-foot or square-meter} {remove comma?} {remove hyphens?} {meter and no and no} {40 tsubo = 132 square meters = 1400 square feet} {but we'll stick to metric system to be consistent}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.39,0:10:24.77,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,The framework alone weighs at least thirty tons!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.77,0:10:27.61,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Get crushed!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.60,0:11:02.31,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}What happened?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.31,0:11:04.81,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}Did I fall into his shadow again?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.40,0:11:09.23,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}No! This is real water!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.23,0:11:10.07,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}How?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.28,0:11:12.36,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}What's this weight?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.36,0:11:15.11,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is that brat trying to strangle me?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.11,0:11:17.41,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}How strong is he?! {CR: What power!}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.41,0:11:19.12,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}No, that's not it!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.12,0:11:22.83,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's from the weight of the two cars I added!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.71,0:11:25.75,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is bad!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.42,0:11:28.04,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}This time, I'm actually drowning!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.84,0:11:31.96,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have to dismiss Contractual Re-Creation!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.44,0:11:51.94,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.94,0:11:53.86,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is a community gymnasium!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.86,0:11:56.99,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}And the basement level has a swimming pool! {heated}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.95,0:12:02.53,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}He fled into his shadow and dismissed his domain,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.53,0:12:06.33,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}forcing me to destroy the floor and plunge into the pool?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.88,0:12:13.09,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,You can't use your receipts \Nwhen they're soaked, can you? {Now your receipts are too wet to use.}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.34,0:12:20.60,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}He waited instead of immediately attacking again.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.60,0:12:24.02,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}He's recovering his technique \Nthat he exhausted with his domain, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.02,0:12:27.94,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Who knows?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.85,0:12:32.48,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,I'm betting you can't summon \N{*}cursed beasts{*shikigami} anymore either, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.82,0:12:35.23,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,That's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.23,0:12:38.28,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,You know what comes next, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.66,0:12:43.37,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}He'll use a {*}cursed beast{*shikigami}. \NSomething other than that dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.37,0:12:45.62,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}None of them can deal a decisive blow.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.62,0:12:47.41,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}Go ahead and try!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.41,0:12:51.17,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}The moment you let up, I'll finish you with a counter!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.72,0:13:46.39,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Those knives weren't nearly enough \Nto take out Divine Dog. {CR: Divine Dog isn't weak enough to let that stop it.} {that = knives} {it's clearly shown in a flashback panel in the manga but that got cut from the anime}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.51,0:13:51.98,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Sorcerers are built on lies, huh? {...deception?} {true that does fit better but i dont wanna change it now}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.24,0:14:11.16,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,The domain, the pool...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.96,0:14:16.17,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,It was all to convince me \Nyou couldn't use that dog anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.59,0:14:21.80,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Sure enough, you didn't flee \Ninto this gymnasium, you lured me into it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.55,0:14:28.35,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,To think I'd let a modern sorcerer, \Nand a brat at that, get the better of me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.18,0:14:33.98,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Even if I wanted to flee, \NNue can't carry people for too long. {Nue can't fly while carrying people for too long.}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.98,0:14:36.11,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,I've struggled with that before.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.99,0:14:45.78,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,What's your relation to {*}Master Tengen{*Tengen-sama}?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.62,0:14:51.41,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Tengen?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.58,0:14:55.17,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Oh, right.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.17,0:15:00.50,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Of course, that shut-in would still be alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.50,0:15:02.34,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,All right. Got it. {CR: Yeah? That's enough.} {why did he tell him to stop talking. it's more like he knows he wont speak so he makes him shut up. but he could've said sth...} {point is he got what he wanted. he's not shutting him up.}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.38,0:15:08.89,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}The goal of the Culling Game, as told by {*}Master Tengen{*Tengen-sama}, \Nwas a misdirect according to Reggie. {it almost read like reggie was calling out tengen for being a liar, which was wrong.}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.43,0:15:16.52,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}I should consider that {*}Master Tengen{*Tengen-sama} and Kenjaku \Nmay be working together and lying to us, {the goal part can be inferred from context. i dont wanna repeat it on the very next line.}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.15,0:15:19.48,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}but that doesn't seem likely from his reaction.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.49,0:15:28.82,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Kogane, give him all my points.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.49,0:15:30.58,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,Okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.16,0:15:36.42,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,You have received 41 points from Reggie Star.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.42,0:15:37.83,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,What are you plotting?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.58,0:15:41.30,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Such an awful thing to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.63,0:15:44.26,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Consider it my last good deed. {It's my good deed before I die.}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.17,0:15:47.80,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,I'm just a spectator.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.80,0:15:50.47,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,I was never close with Kenjaku.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.01,0:15:54.52,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,I have a feeling this'll make things more interesting. {I thought this whole thing might be interesting.} {is he talking about joining the culling game here? or transferring his points?} {could be either. grammatically it leans towards points. thematically tho, it only makes sense for him to reflect on why he agreed to reincarnate in the first place} {besides he answered that points question 3 lines ago} {correction from the future: while this reading makes a ton of thematic sense, it is, in fact, incorrect. on the verge of death, he is not talking about his life choices, but the fucking points giveaway} {maybe the point of the line is to show his "spectator" nature. maybe he signed up for the culling game for similar reasons: curiosity}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.02,0:15:57.19,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Just a hunch, really.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.44,0:16:02.65,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Do me a favor, would you? You did kill me, after all. {he's saying "you killed someone like me" a neutral, curious bystander who just wanted to see how things played out (in the culling game? or after the point transfer?) and even gave you his points on the way out!} {this also supports both readings lmao fuck you gege why are you vagueposting} {i take that back gege i was not familiar with your game}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.44,0:16:10.62,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Let fate toy with you until you become the fool and die. {it's like reggie is projecting his own fate onto megumi. he joined the culling game because he thought it might be interesting, but ended up a pawn toyed with in kenny's game, humiliated himself like a fool losing to a brat, and died} {CR: Let fate toy with you a bit, and die a fool.} {Let fate toy with you, turn you into a clown, and die.} {clown is not the right word here}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.26,0:16:35.89,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,You have scored five points.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.15,0:16:50.28,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,Did I get him?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.91,0:16:52.91,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,No! Don't let your guard down! {glad i wasn't that guy!}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.58,0:16:55.83,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,The enemy is tough! {He's tough!}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.83,0:16:57.41,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,What the hell?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.00,0:17:00.04,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,Why are you covered in lotion?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.04,0:17:01.54,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,It could be sauce.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.54,0:17:03.00,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,Shut up! Die!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.63,0:17:07.13,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,Wait, it really is sauce?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.13,0:17:10.22,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,{\i1}Damn it! What's with this guy?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.22,0:17:12.39,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've blown him up so many times!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.39,0:17:14.89,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,{\i1}I feel like I've killed him five times over!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.89,0:17:17.47,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,{\i1}So why does he have barely any damage?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.73,0:17:20.02,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,You don't like sauce?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.69,0:17:23.27,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,{\i1}His previous injuries have already healed.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.94,0:17:27.78,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,{\i1}But there's no sign of him\Nusing reverse cursed technique like I do.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.69,0:17:30.49,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,{\i1}It makes no sense! {I don't get it!}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.20,0:17:32.53,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,{*}Master Hazenoki{*Hazenoki-sama}.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.53,0:17:33.83,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.83,0:17:37.04,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,{*}Master Reggie Star{*Reggie Star-sama} has just died.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.79,0:17:42.25,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,Oh? What happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.58,0:17:45.09,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,I'm going home. I've had enough of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.09,0:17:46.09,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,Okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.09,0:17:47.30,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,Make sure you take a bath!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.30,0:17:48.46,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,And brush your teeth!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.51,0:17:54.05,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,Hey, man! Gimme your points! {kanchi?} {prolly some weird and obscure reference}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.51,0:17:55.80,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,Stop following me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.80,0:17:59.14,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,C'mon! You know it's customary to leave a tip! {C'mon! Just play along!} {Please! Think of it as going with the flow!} {manga: just for the fun of it} {ofc it's another reference but im not gonna bother typing it out here. look it up.} {since the actual reference wont make sense in eng, let's put something else in place of it. maybe a bad joke or a pun, anything that's not generic "just play along"}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.52,0:18:00.35,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,Die.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.77,0:18:07.90,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Takaba's cursed technique, Comedian, \Nturns whatever he's convinced to be funny into reality.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.90,0:18:11.86,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,It's a technique capable of opposing even Gojo Satoru. {effective against?}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.57,0:18:18.45,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Yet Takaba doesn't know anything \Nabout his own technique.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.88,0:18:28.84,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\i1}I don't get it! I don't get it!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.84,0:18:32.26,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\i1}Ever since I became an adult, \NI hardly understand anything!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.06,0:18:40.77,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\i1}They say all men are wolves,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.77,0:18:44.94,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\i1}but it's always a wolf who takes care \Nof the confusing stuff for me!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.19,0:18:54.70,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\i1}If a wolf will handle everything, \Nthen I don't need to worry about anything!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.70,0:18:57.41,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\i1}Because I'm so cute!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.58,0:19:06.71,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\i1}The wolf will always... {can we not use "..." here?}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.71,0:19:07.67,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\i1}always...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.59,0:19:18.85,Default,Tsumiki,0,0,0,,{\an8\i1}Don't, Megumi.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.19,0:19:27.15,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\an8}You'll spare me?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.57,0:19:37.16,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Shut up.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.62,0:19:42.49,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Stupid sister. {this line just doesn't sit right with me. in s1 he passed out in a similar way after using his domain and called her "stupid sister" (which we changed to "dummy" and might wanna revert) this time he is clearly pissed off, but that still doesn't warrant this i feel.} {i dont wanna think about this rn. later.} {it is now later. i've decided it should just be "stupid sister." s1 will be updated to "stupid sis." it's similar but different enough.}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.22,0:20:05.18,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,{\an8}Things escalated quickly in Sendai Colony.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.18,0:20:10.44,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,{\an8}Far more intense, too, \Nthan anything in the Tokyo Colony.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.77,0:20:17.32,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Dhruv Lakdawalla. 91 points.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.32,0:20:19.07,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,A sorcerer incarnated for the second time. {wait how did he reincarnate twice?}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.95,0:20:25.29,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,He's a veteran who single-handedly conquered \Nthe archipelago during the Civil War of Wa.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.00,0:20:32.59,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,He possesses two autonomous {*}cursed beasts{*shikigami} \Nwhose trajectories define his domain. {the space enclosed by their movement paths becomes his domain.} {we don't know if his domain has a sure-hit attack because back then domains were generally used to enforce rules. still, bro was incarnated once before so he might have picked up that skill. we just don't know for sure.}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.67,0:20:40.01,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Ishigori Ryu. 77 points.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.84,0:20:45.14,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,He's the cannon with the greatest \Ncursed energy output among the players.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.89,0:20:50.44,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Uro Takako. 70 points.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.31,0:20:54.23,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,She was the captain of \Nthe Sun, Moon, and Stars Squad.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.23,0:20:57.28,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,A squad of assassins serving directly \Nunder the Fujiwara Clan.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.28,0:21:00.66,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,She possesses a technique \Nthat allows her to manipulate the sky.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.91,0:21:05.70,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Kurourushi. 54 points.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.12,0:21:12.04,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,It's a cockroach cursed spirit \Nthat Kenjaku freed from Curse Manipulation.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.04,0:21:15.88,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,It ranks as a special-grade, registered officially. {(already registered)} {(???)}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.13,0:21:20.84,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,It's currently lying dormant \Nuntil certain conditions are met.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.34,0:21:23.81,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,There were no alliances.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.81,0:21:30.14,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Their complex compatibility and evenly matched strength \Nput them in a four-way deadlock. {a three—no, }
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.64,0:21:33.36,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,However, one of those pillars
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.86,0:21:36.15,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,has fallen.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.78,0:21:42.32,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Okkotsu Yuta. 35 points.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.16,0:21:48.04,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,He regained his special-grade status \Nthree months after the Night Parade of a Hundred Demons. {blossomed as a special-grade sorcerer.} {special-grade "status" because he was not a special-grade sorcerer before, he was a special-grade cursed human. it's explicitly said he's a sorcerer now but adding that makes room for (mis)interpretation}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.04,0:21:51.54,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,In the modern age, his abilities are \Nsecond only to Gojo Satoru. {CR/manga: He was a modern sorcerer rivaling Gojo Satoru in unusual abilities.} {the narrator has always glazed people to be "second only to gojo satoru" but it always comes with an asterisk. in terms of speed? naobito. in terms of strength? yuki. in terms of potential? higuruma. and in terms of (supernatural) abilities? yuta. he's not the 2nd strongest in general, he just has the 2nd most cracked ability in the modern age: ungodly amount of cursed energy combined with his copy technique} {about supernatural/extraordinary: abilities are inherently extraordinary in jjk but his abilities are extraordinary even among the extraordinary. still, i dont wanna spell it out because the timing is tight and being second to gojo does the job}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.92,0:21:53.38,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,An anomaly. {this whole sequence is glazing yuta and the delivery calls for a mic drop closer so adding "A prodigy." does make sense?} {how about "An anomaly."} {wait that... that actually makes too much sense. because gojo has been referred to as an anomaly several times before, there's even a whole episode titled after this (which got translated as nonstandard but i'll have to fix that ig)}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.51,0:23:28.18,Default,Okkotsu,0,0,0,,{\an8}I'll obtain 400 points all by myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.18,0:23:31.10,Default,Rika,0,0,62,,{\an8}{\fnKG HAPPY Solid\fs81\fscx84\b0}Yuta, what'll it be?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.10,0:23:32.10,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,{\an8}It's called Kurourushi.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.10,0:23:32.81,Default,Okkotsu,0,0,0,,{\an8}Give me everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.81,0:23:35.35,Default,Rika,0,0,62,,{\an8}{\fnKG HAPPY Solid\fs81\fscx84\b0}Give Yuta back!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.35,0:23:38.44,Default,Okkotsu,0,0,0,,{\an8}I won't let you kill your best friend a second time.
